<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.claude.worktree-gc-infra — the SCHEDULED worktree janitor for claude-infrastructure.

  scripts/worktree-gc.sh has been a complete, safe janitor for this repo since 2026-07-25 and
  nothing ever ran it on a cadence: the only scheduled reaper on this box is gl.reso.worktree-gc,
  whose runner hardcodes the reso repo. Measured 2026-08-01: 126 worktrees, 1,193 branches. This
  plist is the missing cron and nothing else — every safety gate stays in worktree-gc.sh.

  04:15, NOT 03:15. reso's reaper owns 03:15, and both sweeps run `git worktree remove` / `git
  branch -d` against repos that share ~/Development/.worktrees; an hour of separation keeps them
  off each other's git objects. (They also share worktree-gc.sh's own CC_WTGC_LOCK default, which
  is the correctness guarantee; the offset is what keeps that lock from turning one sweep into a
  no-op every night.)

  `bash -c` (not a bare ProgramArguments path) for the same reason as deploy-live: launchd expands
  neither ~ nor $HOME inside ProgramArguments. Standard*Path cannot take $HOME at all, hence the
  literals. The script hardens its own PATH on line 1 — including /usr/sbin, where lsof lives and
  whose omission made reso's reaper blind to live sessions and reap one (2026-06-19).

  RunAtLoad false: unlike deploy-live, a stale sweep costs nothing and a login is a moment when
  worktrees are MOST likely to be in use. There is no urgency that justifies reaping at boot.

  THREE TRIGGERS SINCE 2026-10-17 (DESIGN docs/research/load-root-cause-2026-10-17 §3.4 "Wake actuator",
  WP-16), and the script is invoked with `auto` (its double-hyphen flag; see ProgramArguments) on all of them:
    04:15 calendar   the backstop sweep, unchanged.
    WatchPaths       ~/.claude/state/worktree-gc.wake, touched by cc-reaper and branch-prune-landed when they
                     ENQUEUE a tree instead of removing it, and by SessionEnd (hooks/live-session-registry.sh,
                     through wt_emit_event) when a session leaves its worktree. The run takes the queued entries only, O(1) in the
                     population, so the reaper's removals stop being a second janitor racing this one.
    StartInterval    600 s: fires entries whose wake was debounced, and is the fallback if WatchPaths stops
                     delivering during an fseventsd fault. With nothing due it exits in O(1).
  `auto` picks between them: the full backstop when it is due, else the wake run.
  WHY THIS IS SAFE TO GO LIVE ON DEPLOY: this label is `run`, so install.sh reloads the changed plist on the
  next converge with no operator step. What keeps that harmless is in code, not here: the event mode
  defaults to observe (scripts/lib/wtgc-scope.sh), which evaluates and logs would_park / would_detach /
  would_keep with reasons and touches nothing, until the operator's
  docs/activation/pending-activation/52-load-2026-10-17-activate.sh writes `act` to
  ~/.claude/autonomy/worktree-gc-events.mode.

  C10: the OPERATOR loads this, via docs/activation/pending-activation/27-worktree-gc-infra-activate.sh.
  Kill switch (no unload needed): touch ~/.claude/autonomy/worktree-gc-infra.disabled
  Full stop:                      launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.claude.worktree-gc-infra
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.claude.worktree-gc-infra</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>if [ -x /usr/sbin/taskpolicy ]; then exec /usr/sbin/taskpolicy -c utility /usr/bin/env bash "$HOME/.claude/scripts/worktree-gc-infra-run.sh" --auto; fi; exec /usr/bin/env bash "$HOME/.claude/scripts/worktree-gc-infra-run.sh" --auto</string>
    </array>

    <key>WatchPaths</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/state/worktree-gc.wake</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>600</integer>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>4</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>15</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
    <true/>

    <key>Nice</key>
    <integer>10</integer>

    <!--
      NO ProcessType KEY (2026-10-04, docs/research/concurrency-scale-2026-10-04 fix row 5; applied to
      the LOADED job by migrations/0055, an operator step). This job declared `ProcessType Background`,
      which is Darwin's darwinbg task role: every descendant is pinned at PRI 4 and nothing inside
      the job can lift it (com.claude.postland-verify.plist carries the measurement). Measured:
      sweeps took 43-202 minutes.
      ProgramArguments now execs through `taskpolicy -c utility`, the band postland-verify moved to:
      still below interactive sessions, but schedulable. Fail-open: no taskpolicy(8) means exec the
      script directly. LowPriorityIO and Nice stay.
    -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/worktree-gc-infra.out.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/worktree-gc-infra.out.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
